**Read:** Complete the three investigations and assigned full readings. Return to structure, kinetics, mechanics, transport and processing whenever a mechanism assumes an unexplained state or quantity.

Explain electrochemical corrosion, local chemistry, environment-assisted fracture, hydrogen, high-temperature scales, polymer aging/weathering, water and interface effects, glass/ceramic/concrete deterioration, wood decay and contact/flow damage. Reproduce the mixed-potential example and criticize its assumptions. Compare laboratory evidence with service histories, preserving functional criteria and uncertainty.

**Demonstrate:** Defend the three studies, answer a competing interpretation and revise the result. Explain one apparently successful accelerated test that does not support the proposed service conclusion. Connect protection with material state, geometry, environment and monitoring instead of relying on a resistance label.

Continue into material selection, service and recovery: use the degradation evidence when comparing feasible states and preserving useful function.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).

